1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,040
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:04,430
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,430 --> 00:00:05,580
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,030 --> 00:00:08,570
I've been building
cabinets for thirty years.

5
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:09,860
Standing at the workbench

6
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:11,500
on a hard shop floor,

7
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,520
all day long.

8
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,490
I had my right knee
replaced

9
00:00:14,490 --> 00:00:15,610
two years ago.

10
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,950
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:17,990 --> 00:00:19,230
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:20,760
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:21,860
and it went away.

14
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:22,880
This is different.

15
00:00:22,990 --> 00:00:23,530
Tight.

16
00:00:23,570 --> 00:00:24,160
Full.

17
00:00:24,310 --> 00:00:25,190
Like a band around

18
00:00:25,190 --> 00:00:26,900
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:27,840
And for two years I've

20
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:29,020
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:30,040
Give it time.

22
00:00:30,270 --> 00:00:32,090
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:32,090 --> 00:00:33,430
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:34,630
At three months,

25
00:00:34,630 --> 00:00:35,720
give it six.

26
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:36,740
At six months,

27
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:38,430
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:38,690 --> 00:00:39,340
At a year,

29
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:41,120
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:42,450
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:42,490 --> 00:00:43,910
We went down the list.

32
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:45,460
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:46,710
Every session,

34
00:00:46,710 --> 00:00:48,230
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:49,660
I got stronger.

36
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:51,210
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:51,270 --> 00:00:52,820
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:54,170
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:54,210 --> 00:00:56,350
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:56,350 --> 00:00:57,400
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:58,380
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:00,030
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:00,110 --> 00:01:02,150
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:02,430 --> 00:01:03,840
And after that, a second

45
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:05,650
operation to go back in

46
00:01:05,650 --> 00:01:06,650
and do it over.

47
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:07,800
I said no.

48
00:01:08,110 --> 00:01:09,840
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:10,760
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:12,580
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:15,110
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:16,820
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:17,780
for it and went out

54
00:01:17,780 --> 00:01:18,630
to the shop.

55
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:20,360
Couldn't do the stairs,

56
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:21,430
couldn't stand at the
counter

57
00:01:21,430 --> 00:01:23,140
long enough to finish
dinner,

58
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:25,020
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

59
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:26,930
without shifting every two
minutes.

60
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,180
At the shop,

61
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:29,500
I'd lean on the bench just

62
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:31,130
to take the weight off
that leg.

63
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:32,330
The young guy who works

64
00:01:32,330 --> 00:01:33,890
for me started carrying
the lumber.

65
00:01:34,110 --> 00:01:35,400
Nobody said anything.

66
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,060
It woke me at night,

67
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:38,840
and it turned ordinary
things,

68
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:40,080
like getting in the truck

69
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:41,440
or up off the couch,

70
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,550
into a decision.

71
00:01:42,990 --> 00:01:44,420
After a long and serious

72
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:45,670
talk with my wife,

73
00:01:45,670 --> 00:01:47,550
I went back in one more
time.

74
00:01:47,890 --> 00:01:49,010
That was the fourth set

75
00:01:49,010 --> 00:01:50,630
of X-rays on this knee.

76
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:52,180
And like the three before
it,

77
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:54,970
the answer was everything
looks great.

78
00:01:55,010 --> 00:01:57,170
No loosening, no
infection,

79
00:01:57,170 --> 00:01:58,280
nothing wrong.

80
00:01:58,390 --> 00:01:59,670
Only this time

81
00:01:59,670 --> 00:02:01,090
there was no new number.

82
00:02:01,210 --> 00:02:03,730
Nobody said give it
another six months.

83
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:05,480
There was nothing left to
give it.

84
00:02:05,690 --> 00:02:06,740
I sat in the parking

85
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:07,900
lot for a while.

86
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:09,470
Okay, I thought.

87
00:02:09,530 --> 00:02:10,870
Then explain this.

88
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:13,270
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

89
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:14,720
I hit my breaking point.

90
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:17,090
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

91
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:19,220
Everyone in the house was
asleep

92
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:20,970
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

93
00:02:20,970 --> 00:02:22,070
with my leg up,

94
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:23,710
trying to find any angle
where

95
00:02:23,710 --> 00:02:25,310
it didn't feel like
something was wrapped

96
00:02:25,310 --> 00:02:27,350
around my knee and
tightening.

97
00:02:27,670 --> 00:02:29,980
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

98
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:31,780
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

99
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:32,750
I had a kitchen

100
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:34,120
to install that week.

101
00:02:34,330 --> 00:02:35,590
And I just thought,

102
00:02:35,590 --> 00:02:37,370
is this really my life
now?

103
00:02:37,410 --> 00:02:39,000
I can't live like this.

104
00:02:39,070 --> 00:02:40,710
So I made myself a
promise.

105
00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:42,100
I wouldn't go a day

106
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:43,710
without looking for an
answer.

107
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,220
And when I found one,

108
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:46,330
I'd share it with everyone

109
00:02:46,330 --> 00:02:47,680
going through the same
thing.

110
00:02:47,970 --> 00:02:49,040
So I got my laptop

111
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,160
out and went looking.

112
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,480
Not for a product.

113
00:02:51,570 --> 00:02:52,690
For an explanation.

114
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:54,600
Mayo Clinic forums,

115
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:56,870
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

116
00:02:56,870 --> 00:02:59,700
doctor videos, medical
animations.

117
00:02:59,970 --> 00:03:01,260
And that's when I found a
video

118
00:03:01,260 --> 00:03:03,140
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

119
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:04,600
Steven Salinger,

120
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,080
whose own wife had been

121
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,500
through exactly this.

122
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:10,050
But before I say anything
else,

123
00:03:10,050 --> 00:03:11,460
I want to be straight with
you.

124
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:14,030
You've already had
something work fast.

125
00:03:14,130 --> 00:03:15,010
The ice.

126
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:16,780
The first week of a new
pill.

127
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,390
The good day after a
session.

128
00:03:18,430 --> 00:03:19,760
Then it wore off.

129
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:21,960
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

130
00:03:22,270 --> 00:03:24,430
Fast relief isn't relief.

131
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:25,890
It's a preview.

132
00:03:26,370 --> 00:03:27,430
So I'm not going to tell

133
00:03:27,430 --> 00:03:28,470
you this works fast.

134
00:03:28,510 --> 00:03:29,460
It doesn't.

135
00:03:29,650 --> 00:03:31,500
But if you're willing to
be patient,

136
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:32,690
and to look at what's
going

137
00:03:32,690 --> 00:03:33,870
on around your new knee

138
00:03:33,870 --> 00:03:35,570
instead of inside it,
there

139
00:03:35,570 --> 00:03:37,680
is a real reason it still
hurts.

140
00:03:37,850 --> 00:03:39,630
And something you can do
about it.

141
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:41,450
Let me explain what he
said,

142
00:03:41,450 --> 00:03:42,760
because this is what
changed

143
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:43,860
everything for me.

144
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:45,680
He started with the
basics.

145
00:03:45,830 --> 00:03:47,300
A knee replacement takes
out

146
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:48,920
the worn joint surfaces

147
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,620
and puts in metal and
plastic.

148
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:52,680
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

149
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:54,200
you had before the
operation.

150
00:03:54,390 --> 00:03:55,660
That part I already knew.

151
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:57,020
But then he explained
something

152
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:57,980
nobody had ever told me.

153
00:03:58,020 --> 00:03:58,400
He said,

154
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,680
think about a swollen foot

155
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:00,870
inside a shoe.

156
00:04:00,970 --> 00:04:02,420
The shoe didn't shrink.

157
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:04,700
Your foot is taking up
more room,

158
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:06,340
so everything feels
cramped

159
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:07,700
and tight and squeezed.

160
00:04:08,030 --> 00:04:08,980
Your new knee sits

161
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:10,380
in a limited space with
living

162
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:11,900
tissue packed all around
it.

163
00:04:12,310 --> 00:04:14,450
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

164
00:04:14,450 --> 00:04:16,400
had to work through that
tissue.

165
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:19,460
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

166
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:21,360
At first that's normal.

167
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:23,300
But in some people that
swelling can

168
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:26,070
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

169
00:04:26,210 --> 00:04:28,110
And swollen tissue takes
up more

170
00:04:28,110 --> 00:04:30,050
room than calm tissue
does.

171
00:04:30,090 --> 00:04:30,820
So when you bend,

172
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:32,580
that tissue gets
compressed.

173
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:33,960
When you straighten,

174
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:35,230
it gets pulled tight.

175
00:04:35,270 --> 00:04:36,380
That's the band.

176
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:38,570
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

177
00:04:38,610 --> 00:04:39,480
And you start being

178
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:40,550
the one who says,

179
00:04:40,550 --> 00:04:41,620
you go ahead.

180
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:42,720
I'll stay here.

181
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:44,910
And that's exactly why so
much

182
00:04:44,910 --> 00:04:46,920
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

183
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,940
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

184
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:49,930
around the knee.

185
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:51,520
Worth doing,

186
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:52,550
and I'd done it.

187
00:04:53,010 --> 00:04:54,770
It does nothing about
tissue

188
00:04:54,770 --> 00:04:55,970
taking up room.

189
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:57,370
A nerve block quiets

190
00:04:57,370 --> 00:04:59,160
the nerve carrying the
signal.

191
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:01,880
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

192
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,740
But when that irritated
tissue

193
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:05,330
finally calms down,

194
00:05:05,330 --> 00:05:06,930
it holds less fluid,

195
00:05:06,930 --> 00:05:08,530
and it takes up less room.

196
00:05:08,650 --> 00:05:11,280
Less room taken up means
less pressure

197
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:12,640
squeezing the joint.

198
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:14,430
That's what takes the
pressure off.

199
00:05:14,710 --> 00:05:16,200
After two years of this,

200
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,780
it finally made sense.

201
00:05:18,110 --> 00:05:20,030
The problem was never the
new knee.

202
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:22,060
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

203
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:23,920
He calls it the squeeze.

204
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:26,430
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

205
00:05:26,710 --> 00:05:28,400
I'd bought knee sleeves,

206
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:29,820
anti-fatigue mats,

207
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:32,250
compression braces,
creams,

208
00:05:32,250 --> 00:05:34,050
half of Amazon really,

209
00:05:34,050 --> 00:05:35,270
and all any of it gave

210
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:36,340
me was an hour.

211
00:05:36,410 --> 00:05:37,310
I even looked at going

212
00:05:37,310 --> 00:05:39,040
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

213
00:05:39,210 --> 00:05:40,870
But at $200 a session

214
00:05:40,870 --> 00:05:42,960
with nothing covered by
insurance,

215
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:44,250
that was a quick no.

216
00:05:44,870 --> 00:05:46,320
Then one night I went back

217
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:48,080
to that knee replacement
group

218
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:49,170
and actually read it.

219
00:05:49,490 --> 00:05:51,140
Thousands of people,

220
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:52,650
years out from surgery,

221
00:05:52,650 --> 00:05:55,460
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

222
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:56,880
nobody could explain.

223
00:05:57,010 --> 00:05:59,130
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

224
00:05:59,130 --> 00:06:00,790
the same thing kept coming
up.

225
00:06:00,830 --> 00:06:02,690
This one device,

226
00:06:02,690 --> 00:06:04,950
and people saying it was
the first

227
00:06:04,950 --> 00:06:07,200
thing that made a
difference.

228
00:06:07,590 --> 00:06:09,850
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

229
00:06:09,850 --> 00:06:11,430
alright, here it comes,

230
00:06:11,430 --> 00:06:13,010
he's selling me something,

231
00:06:13,010 --> 00:06:14,860
let me shut that down
right now.

232
00:06:15,050 --> 00:06:16,890
I'm only here because I
made myself

233
00:06:16,890 --> 00:06:19,140
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

234
00:06:19,140 --> 00:06:20,200
that if I ever found

235
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,390
something that helped,

236
00:06:21,390 --> 00:06:22,410
I'd say so.

237
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:24,390
It's called the KenRelief
Red

238
00:06:24,390 --> 00:06:25,740
Light Therapy Wrap.

239
00:06:25,890 --> 00:06:27,870
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

240
00:06:28,150 --> 00:06:30,370
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

241
00:06:30,370 --> 00:06:32,810
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

242
00:06:33,130 --> 00:06:35,020
But I went to their
website anyway,

243
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:35,910
just to see what all

244
00:06:35,910 --> 00:06:37,210
the fuss was about.

245
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:40,550
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

246
00:06:40,550 --> 00:06:43,630
charge $200 a session for,

247
00:06:43,630 --> 00:06:46,750
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

248
00:06:46,750 --> 00:06:47,840
in a wrap you plug

249
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:49,180
into the wall at home.

250
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:50,950
Two hundred and forty
lights.

251
00:06:51,110 --> 00:06:53,040
Red at 660 nanometers

252
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:55,360
and near-infrared at 850,

253
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:57,560
run together for the
strongest effect.

254
00:06:57,650 --> 00:06:59,030
Four strength levels.

255
00:06:59,070 --> 00:07:01,000
A five to thirty minute
timer.

256
00:07:01,070 --> 00:07:02,560
Then I saw the guarantee.

257
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:03,750
Ninety days.

258
00:07:03,830 --> 00:07:05,630
Results or your money
back,

259
00:07:05,630 --> 00:07:08,060
no questions, no store
credit,

260
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,810
and you don't even send it
back.

261
00:07:10,330 --> 00:07:12,780
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

262
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:14,360
days to change my mind.

263
00:07:14,570 --> 00:07:16,090
There wasn't much to lose,

264
00:07:16,090 --> 00:07:17,230
so I ordered it.

265
00:07:17,460 --> 00:07:18,740
Two of them, actually.

266
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:21,320
Only the right knee was
replaced,

267
00:07:21,320 --> 00:07:23,560
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

268
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,750
and I'd done it at the
bench

269
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:25,880
for two years.

270
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:28,180
The left one was carrying
the difference.

271
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:29,230
When it came,

272
00:07:29,230 --> 00:07:31,400
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

273
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:32,680
because I'd been let down
too

274
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,270
many times to get excited.

275
00:07:34,510 --> 00:07:36,230
What I felt was warmth.

276
00:07:36,270 --> 00:07:38,130
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

277
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:39,980
More like it was coming
from inside

278
00:07:39,980 --> 00:07:42,000
the knee and spreading
around it.

279
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:43,090
And that was it.

280
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:45,000
That was the whole
experience.

281
00:07:45,110 --> 00:07:46,430
